#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:1
msgid "Friendly Admonitions"
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:3
msgid ""
"`just` will happily skip cached recipes, but it is your responsibility to "
"make sure that this is safe, and that the contents of the cache key capture "
"enough information about recipe invocations for caching to make sense in the "
"first place."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:8
msgid ""
"In particular, there are many details about the context in which a recipe "
"runs that are not captured by cache keys."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:11
msgid ""
"These include the time, input files, output files, system binaries, "
"operating system version, databases, systems over the network, the DNS, and "
"any of the myriad other things which may change the execution of a computer "
"program."
msgstr ""

#: src/friendly-admonitions.md:15
msgid ""
"Attempting to skip execution based on the type of crude heuristics that "
"`just` employs has a long and sordid history. However, it is an undeniably "
"convenient and powerful tool, and it is provided in the hopes that you find "
"it useful."
msgstr ""
